 ],
 "text": "What if every container ship on Earth stopped for 30 days? Not slowed down, stopped. Around 80% of world trade by volume moves by sea, according to the United Nations. Day 1. Ships drop anchor outside every major port, from Rotterdam to Shanghai to Los Angeles. Crews wait for orders that never come, insurers start making very nervous phone calls. We've seen a tiny version of this before. In 2021, one ship, the Ever Given, got stuck in the Suez Canal for six days. It held up about $9.6 billion of goods every single day. Week 1. Factories run out of parts. A car plant stops the whole line because one small ship is missing. Phone makers send workers home. Week 2. Ports go quiet. Thousands of trucks sit in the yard with nothing to pick up. Drivers start looking for other work. DHO Month 1. Shelves thin out, prices climb, and every brand finds out how many weeks of stock it really has. Most find out it's fewer than they thought. How many weeks could your business last? Tell us in the comments."
}